      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 180C. Grease and line two 20cm round tins. Coarsely grate about 300g of peeled carrots (roughly 3 large carrots)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk together the oil, both sugars, and eggs until combined. Sift in the flour, baking powder, bicarb, and spices. Fold together. Stir in the grated carrot."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide between the two tins. Bake for 35 to 40 minutes until a skewer comes out clean. Cool in the tins for 10 minutes, then turn out."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For the frosting: beat the cream cheese and softened butter together. Sift in the icing sugar and beat until smooth and spreadable."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Sandwich the cooled layers with half the frosting. Spread the rest over the top. Refrigerate for at least 30 minutes before slicing."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Cake is dense and heavy",
              "cause": "Batter over-mixed once the flour was added.",
              "fix": "Fold the dry ingredients in gently. Stop as soon as the flour disappears."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Frosting is too runny to spread",
              "cause": "Cream cheese was too warm.",
              "fix": "Refrigerate the frosting for 20 minutes before spreading. Cold cream cheese frosting is much easier to work with."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Carrot cake became fashionable in Britain during the 1970s, partly because it was marketed as a healthier option. The cream cheese frosting is an American addition. Today it appears in virtually every British cafe and is one of the bestselling cakes in the country. It keeps better than most cakes and is excellent for several days after baking."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
